    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-14624",
      "problem": "Let $A = \\mathbb{R},$ and consider the relation $R$ on $A$ such that $x \\: R \\: y$ if and only if $x$ and $y$ both lie above the upward-opening parabola whose focus is at $\\left(0,\\dfrac14\\right)$ and whose vertex is at $O.$ Express $R$ using set-builder notation.",
      "worked_solution": "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A = A^2.$\n\n$$\nR\\subseteq A\\times A\n$$\n\nFor a relation $R$ on a set $A,$ we also have the following notations:\n\n- $a \\: R \\: b$ if and only if $(a,b) \\in R$\n\n- $a \\: \\cancel{\\!R\\!} \\: b$ if and only if $(a,b) \\notin R$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y) \\in \\mathbb{R} \\times \\mathbb{R} = \\mathbb{R}^2$ such that $y \\gt x^2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14117308/assets/26671c4dc03b13afc43172e486602bf3d647f8be911769c24a9e0523f591b64b.png)\n\nTherefore, we can write out $R$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nR = \\Big\\{ (x,y) \\in \\mathbb{R}^2 \\: : \\: y \\gt x^2 \\Big\\}\n$$",
      "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14117308/observations/step-e14624-4b390df90004851e71a7.html",
